    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 101043\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n243 AM PST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Quiet and pleasant conditions anticipated through Friday.\n\n* Cooler conditions and a chance of showers returns late Friday\n  into Saturday, with a stronger system poised to affect the\n  region early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through next Tuesday.\n\nPleasant and mild conditions will continue through most of the\nweek as a large ridge of high pressure expands across the Western\nUS. This will allow temperatures to remain several degrees above\nnormal through Thursday with generally light winds. Exception will\nbe along the Colorado River Valley where sporadic northerly\nbreezes will remain focused as surface high pressure builds across\nthe Great Basin. \n\nChanges begin to arrive late week into the weekend as a closed low\napproaches off the Eastern Pacific. The general expectation is \nfor this low to remain to the south of the International border, \nkeeping its impacts to our region limited. However, it will be \nnudged along by a stronger shortwave that scrapes northern \nCalifornia and the Great Basin Friday night into Saturday. This \nsecondary wave will bring chances for light snow in the Sierra, \nas well as some shower potential to the region, mainly for areas \nnorth of I-40. Thereafter, shortwave ridging will build back in by\nlate Saturday into Sunday before a stronger trough arrives early \nnext week with renewed shower potential.\n\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Winds \nremain light and generally follow typical, daily patterns. Chances \nfor 10+ knots are 10% or less throughout the TAF period. High clouds \nclear out this afternoon.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light winds below 10 \nknots anticipated over most of the region today, generally following \ntypical, daily patterns. The exception is the lower Colorado River \nValley (primarily KIFP to KEED) where speeds 8-14 knots and gusts \naround 20 knots are likely (75%). These breezes will stay elevated \ntonight and into Wednesday. Few to scattered high clouds this \nmorning, clearing from west to east later today.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Outler\nAVIATION...Woods\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
